{
 "config": {
  "stepGap": 200
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "log": "DFM-Rscu 0.6.1125b steering home into a strong wind (fixture rscu-wind: about 14 m/s airspeed into 11.3 m/s of wind, 2.7 m/s over the ground, like Harry's flight of 2026-11-25), computed heading. Into the wind the course turns about 5x faster than the nose, so the steering is too strong: with the old settings the model weaves. 'Heading from GPS' = Fit 6 m and 'Cruise speed' = 50 km/h (steering reduced below that ground speed) must hold it steady. Steering law Curves throughout (this is the 1125b fix; the bank-angle law is tested in rscu-assist-leg)"
  },
  {
   "waitForm": true
  },
  {
   "waitSub": 1
  },
  {
   "wait": 3000
  },
  {
   "expectState": "rscu.zeroLat"
  },
  {
   "setInput": "SA",
   "value": -1
  },
  {
   "link": "App Settings"
  },
  {
   "waitSub": 10
  },
  {
